==Battleground==
*3 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 3~6 seconds<sup>90f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'Solar]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**10 [[Zuche]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**10 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 1.33~2.67 seconds<sup>40f~80f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Focus on bringing [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] cats such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] as the GreGories are the main threat in this stage. Once both the GreGories die, you are likely to win as the Le'Solar has very low HP.

Bring [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] or [[Trash Cat (Special Cat)|Trash Cat]] to get rid of the Zuches. The Zuches and Thrillerz are minor threats, so bringing one or two will suffice. Due to all of The Thrillerz, [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] is excellent here.

If you own a Lv.40 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with [[Explosion]] [[Talents]], you can send him out for a quicker win.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Sarukani]]: Essentially a second, less expensive version of Li'l Flying Cat with better stats all across the board. If you own them, bring them.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Targets both of the main traits here, and provides good coverate all across the board.

